{"type":"npc","name":"Matsugami","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":415,"temp":0,"max":415,"details":""},"ac":{"value":41,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":50,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"swim","value":50}],"details":""},"weaknesses":[{"type":"cold-iron","value":15,"exceptions":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common","draconic","jotun","spirituan","thalassic"],"details":"Telepathy 100 feet"},"level":{"value":18},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Matsugami, also known as ocean kami, are gregarious spirits who protect shorelines and the settlements that inevitably sprout up along them. To a matsugami, fishers are just as much a part of the natural ecosystem as fish. They are fascinated by the cultures within the coastal communities they watch over, as well as by travelers who sail over the ocean to reach them.</p><p>Though matsugami are rare, their existence is no secret to the communities they protect, with locals happily sharing stories of these kami running across the ocean's surface to flying kick a hungry sea serpent or tossing armfuls of beached sea life back to the oceans. When great storms arrive, matsugami patrol the seas, guiding ships to port and hauling people cast overboard back to safety. Communities fortunate enough to enjoy a matsugami's protection typically construct a shrine in their honor, where they leave prayers and offerings.</p><h2>Teach Someone to Fish...</h2><p>Despite their reputation as boisterous guardians, matsugami are patient with troublemakers. They prefer to educate and negotiate, only resorting to violence against those who threaten the safety of their ward.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 3,000/7,000/13,000 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), armor (light), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Diplomacy, Medicine, Nature, Religion, Society, Stealth)</p><p><strong>Eligible I